ASoC: Intel: bytcr_rt5651: Add quirk for Chuwi Vi8 Plus with unfilled DMI

Some Chuwi Vi8 Plus (CWI519) units report "To be filled by O.E.M." for both
sys_vendor and product_name, so the existing Vi8 Plus quirk cannot match and
the mono-speaker, swapped-headphone and IN2 microphone corrections are not
applied.

Add a second entry keyed on the board fields plus the BIOS date, carrying the
same quirk flags as the existing entry.

Signed-off-by: Your Name <your.email@example.com>
---
 Generated against linux master 3eb40771c00a (2026-08-15).
 Apply with: git am, or patch -p1 < this file
---
--- a/sound/soc/intel/boards/bytcr_rt5651.c
+++ b/sound/soc/intel/boards/bytcr_rt5651.c
@@ -416,6 +416,20 @@
 		.matches = {
 			DMI_MATCH(DMI_SYS_VENDOR, "Hampoo"),
 			DMI_MATCH(DMI_PRODUCT_NAME, "D2D3_Vi8A1"),
+		},
+		.driver_data = (void *)(BYT_RT5651_DEFAULT_QUIRKS |
+					BYT_RT5651_IN2_MAP |
+					BYT_RT5651_HP_LR_SWAPPED |
+					BYT_RT5651_MONO_SPEAKER),
+	},
+	{
+		/* Chuwi Vi8 Plus (CWI519), unit with unfilled system DMI */
+		.callback = byt_rt5651_quirk_cb,
+		.matches = {
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_BOARD_VENDOR, "Hampoo"),
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_BOARD_NAME, "Cherry Trail CR"),
+			/* Above matches are too generic, add bios-date match */
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_BIOS_DATE, "12/11/2015"),
 		},
 		.driver_data = (void *)(BYT_RT5651_DEFAULT_QUIRKS |
 					BYT_RT5651_IN2_MAP |
